WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.775
&gt;&gt; Amorpha fruticosa, indigo -
bush or just Amorpha, common name.

00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:08.670
This is a large shrubby plant found

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.805
along lake shores, freshwater lakes.

00:00:11.805 --> 00:00:15.150
Its ID feature is its
tremendously long,

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.370
very small pinnate compound
leaflets that are very ubiquitous.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.690
They're just flower in

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.780
an awful brown purple
flower late in the summer,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.330
but you can just cut it
back and it comes back from

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.045
the ground to about
four feet every year.

00:00:30.045 --> 00:00:32.830
It's Amorpha fruticosa.

